        "q": "Can one person connect two Fitbit accounts at the same time?",
        "a": "Only if your schema has somewhere to put the second one. It happens for real reasons: a work wellness account alongside a personal one, or an account created before a signup the user forgot about. Model it as two provider_account rows and two connection rows under the same user. The important follow-on is that the two accounts are not duplicates of each other, they are two honest sources measuring the same person, so your aggregation has to pick a source per interval using a per-user, per-metric priority rather than summing them. Summing is how you get a 34,000-step day."
